(2120560, 290277, 19831, '<td valign="top">A cool shot. Especially for this challenge. Great mood set overall. I like how the shadow goes from the floor to vertically on the cabinets. Neat how, even in the whole dark, bleak setting, the shadow still stands out prominently. Nice job!</td>', 'A cool shot. Especially for this challenge. Great mood set overall. I like how the shadow goes from the floor to vertically on the cabinets. Neat how, even in the whole dark, bleak setting, the shadow still stands out prominently. Nice job!', '2006-02-04 01:06:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2120575, 290277, 44172, '<td valign="top">That looks like Joey Lawrence. I''ve been trying to look at this image without thinking of any of your other work to bias me. I''ve decided that I''d still love it if I knew nothing of you.  It would still be one of my favorites in the group and here''s why... I''m liking the photos that are a composition of more than just the shadow and you have captured that here. The placing of the chair and the stack of paint cans and the background clutter - especially the red items up on top - it doesn''t look deliberate - it all seems very naturally placed - but I know you probably did place everything just so on purpose - to lead the eye around the image in just the right way.  Or at the very least, recognized that all that stuff looked good the way it already was - I don''t know - maybe you were just lazy and didn''t want to move anything out of the way - whatever the reason - it worked well.  Coloring, focus, lighting, it has it all - especially, as usual, the superb processing.  Your pose is great as is the title and of course, it meets the challenge.  I''m not sure if it''s the most creative in the lot - but I do know it''s the best quality as far as layout and processing goes. You certainly don''t <i>need</i> any more ribbons - but this image is very worthy of one.</td>', 'That looks like Joey Lawrence. I''ve been trying to look at this image without thinking of any of your other work to bias me. I''ve decided that I''d still love it if I knew nothing of you.  It would still be one of my favorites in the group and here''s why... I''m liking the photos that are a composition of more than just the shadow and you have captured that here. The placing of the chair and the stack of paint cans and the background clutter - especially the red items up on top - it doesn''t look deliberate - it all seems very naturally placed - but I know you probably did place everything just so on purpose - to lead the eye around the image in just the right way.  Or at the very least, recognized that all that stuff looked good the way it already was - I don''t know - maybe you were just lazy and didn''t want to move anything out of the way - whatever the reason - it worked well.  Coloring, focus, lighting, it has it all - especially, as usual, the superb processing.  Your pose is great as is the title and of course, it meets the challenge.  I''m not sure if it''s the most creative in the lot - but I do know it''s the best quality as far as layout and processing goes. You certainly don''t need any more ribbons - but this image is very worthy of one.', '2006-02-04 01:11:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2120578, 289976, 44172, '<td valign="top">This is one of my very favorites in the entire lot - like the processing, the coloring - and of course - the idea - nice work Batman :)</td>', 'This is one of my very favorites in the entire lot - like the processing, the coloring - and of course - the idea - nice work Batman :)', '2006-02-04 01:12:55.000000', NULL, 1),
